1. What caching actually is

Caching = storing precomputed/frequently-used data closer to computation.
Reduce latency
Reduce DB load
Increase throughput

DB bottlenecks:

disk I/O
locks
connection limits
expensive joins
aggregation
repeated reads

SELECT * FROM products WHERE id = 10;
If requested 50k/sec:

DB melts
CPU spikes
buffer pool churn
lock contention increases

When to bring cache in the interview ?
If your system is read heavy (Reduce the load on db)
To reduce the latency
Expensive query precompute

