A. Client-side cache
Browser/mobile cache.

B. CDN cache (Cloudflare)
Edge locations cache static assets.
images
JS bundles
videos

C. Application cache (backend)
Redis
Memcached

D. Database cache
buffer pool
query cache
page cache

E. Distributed cache
Redis 

Why query becomes faster second time?
Because pages are in memory.

C. Local Caching
Cache stored inside application memory.
const cache = new Map();

Easy and extremely fast.
Problem:
Each server has its own cache.
Server A cache != Server B cache
Cache is also lost after restart/deployment.

D. Distributed Caching (Redis / Memcached)
Centralized cache shared across all servers.
App Servers -> Redis -> Database

Common tools:
Redis
Memcached

Advantages:
Shared cache across instances
Reduces DB load
Better consistency

Problem:
Network latency
Cache invalidation complexity
Extra infrastructure dependency

Redis is more commonly used because it supports:
TTL
Pub/Sub
Distributed locks
Persistence
Advanced data structures

