Redis is famous for single threaded at least for command execustion. 
CPUs today have multiple cores then why redis has single thread. 
Threads aren't free. The coordination between threads: locks, synchronization and context-switching are very expensive. Wastes more CPU cycle than it saves.

How redis handles so many requests in a single thread 
1. Pure ram 
2. Tiny operations 
3. Event loop 


 
